    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-citizenship-cessation-act-2020-sch-1-sec-36b-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "36B(5) Citizenship cessation determination for certain conduct",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-amendment-citizenship-cessation-act-2020#sch-1-sec-36b-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-citizenship-amendment-citizenship-cessation-act-2020.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-citizenship-amendment-citizenship-cessation-act-2020.pdf, p.8",
      "values:originalText": "(5) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(a), the conduct is any of the\nfollowing:\n\n(a) engaging in international terrorist activities using explosive\nor lethal devices;\n\n(b) engaging in a terrorist act;\n\n(c) providing or receiving training connected with preparation\nfor, engagement in, or assistance in a terrorist act;\n\n(d) directing the activities of a terrorist organisation;\n\n(e) recruiting for a terrorist organisation;\n\n(f) financing terrorism;\n\n(g) financing a terrorist;\n\n(h) engaging in foreign incursions and recruitment;\n\n(i) fighting for, or being in the service of, a declared terrorist\norganisation (see section 36C);\n\n(j) serving in the armed forces of a country at war with\nAustralia.\nNote 1:\nA determination may be made in relation to conduct specified in\nsubsection (5) that was engaged in before the subsection commenced\n(see item 18 of Schedule 1 to the Australian Citizenship Amendment\n(Citizenship Cessation) Act 2020).\nNote 2:\nThis section does not apply to conduct of Australian law enforcement\nor intelligence bodies, or to conduct in the course of certain duties to\nthe Commonwealth (see subsection (8)).\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments",
      "skos:definition": "(5) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(a), the conduct is any of the\nfollowing:\n\n(a) engaging in international terrorist activities using explosive\nor lethal devices;\n\n(b) engaging in a terrorist act;\n\n(c) providing or receiving training connected with preparation\nfor, engagement in, or assistance in a terrorist act;\n\n(d) directing the activities of a terrorist organisation;\n\n(e) recruiting for a terrorist organisation;\n\n(f) financing terrorism;\n\n(g) financing a terrorist;\n\n(h) engaging in foreign incursions and recruitment;\n\n(i) fighting for, or being in the service of, a declared terrorist\norganisation (see section 36C);\n\n(j) serving in the armed forces of a country at war with\nAustralia.\nNote 1:\nA determination may be made in relation to conduct specified in\nsubsection (5) that was engaged in before the subsection commenced\n(see item 18 of Schedule 1 to the Australian Citizenship Amendment\n(Citizenship Cessation) Act 2020).\nNote 2:\nThis section does not apply to conduct of Australian law enforcement\nor intelligence bodies, or to conduct in the course of certain duties to\nthe Commonwealth (see subsection (8)).\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-citizenship-cessation-act-2020-sch-1-sec-36b"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-citizenship-cessation-act-2020-sch-1-sec-36b-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
