        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-citizenship-cessation-act-2020-sch-1-sec-36d-ss-1-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-citizenship-cessation-act-2020-sch-1-sec-36d-ss-1-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-citizenship-cessation-act-2020-sch-1-sec-36d-ss-1-logic-deontic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-citizenship-cessation-act-2020-sch-1-sec-36d-ss-1-logic-deontic-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "3b803142bbe71915ff26587887c7b8e5a01d1c4b2036ff48892428fad5c7baeb",
      "skos:note": "Ceases citizenship for certain convictions"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-amendment-citizenship-cessation-act-2020#sch-1-sec-36d-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "36D(1) Citizenship cessation determination for certain convictions",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 12,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may determine in writing that a person ceases to be\nan Australian citizen if:\n\n(a) the person has been convicted of an offence, or offences,\nagainst one or more of the provisions specified in\nsubsection (5); and\n\n(b) the person has, in respect of the conviction or convictions,\nbeen sentenced to a period of imprisonment of at least 3\nyears, or to periods of imprisonment that total at least 3\nyears; and\n\n(c) the Minister is satisfied that the conduct of the person to\nwhich the conviction or convictions relate demonstrates that\nthe person has repudiated their allegiance to Australia; and\n\n(d) the Minister is satisfied that it would be contrary to the public\ninterest for the person to remain an Australian citizen (see\nsection 36E).\nNote:\nA person may seek review of a determination made under this\nsubsection in the High Court of Australia under section 75 of the\nConstitution, or in the Federal Court of Australia under section 39B of\nthe Judiciary Act 1903. See also section 36H of this Act (revocation of\ncitizenship cessation determination on application to Minister)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-citizenship-cessation-act-2020-sch-1-sec-36d-ss-1-norm",
