    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-citizenship-cessation-act-2020-sch-1-sec-36f-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "36F(4) Notice of citizenship cessation",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-amendment-citizenship-cessation-act-2020#sch-1-sec-36f-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-citizenship-amendment-citizenship-cessation-act-2020.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-citizenship-amendment-citizenship-cessation-act-2020.pdf, p.15",
      "values:originalText": "(4) Despite subsection (2), the Minister may give the notice by sending\nit to an electronic address for the person without sending it in\naccordance with that subsection if:\n\n(a) the Minister becomes aware of the electronic address for the\nperson while a determination is in force under\nsubsection 36G(1) (that notice should not be given to the\nperson); and\n\n(b) that determination is revoked.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments",
      "skos:definition": "(4) Despite subsection (2), the Minister may give the notice by sending\nit to an electronic address for the person without sending it in\naccordance with that subsection if:\n\n(a) the Minister becomes aware of the electronic address for the\nperson while a determination is in force under\nsubsection 36G(1) (that notice should not be given to the\nperson); and\n\n(b) that determination is revoked.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-citizenship-cessation-act-2020-sch-1-sec-36f"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
