        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-citizenship-cessation-act-2020-sch-1-sec-36f-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "05c3c7526255f973e31d2f5fc7b321a7671dfb1a4ea6a4476ee4347809db2659",
      "skos:note": "Minister may give notice by electronic address under certain conditions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-amendment-citizenship-cessation-act-2020#sch-1-sec-36f-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "36F(4) Notice of citizenship cessation",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 15,
      "values:originalText": "(4) Despite subsection (2), the Minister may give the notice by sending\nit to an electronic address for the person without sending it in\naccordance with that subsection if:\n\n(a) the Minister becomes aware of the electronic address for the\nperson while a determination is in force under\nsubsection 36G(1) (that notice should not be given to the\nperson); and\n\n(b) that determination is revoked.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-citizenship-cessation-act-2020-sch-1-sec-36f-ss-4-norm",
