        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "55904af495ec679de40eb3d9584a53a025f20633ca10253e5d85bc65cf4dae14",
      "skos:note": "The Minister must give the person written notice of the decision.",
      "dc:description": "written notice"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-amendment-citizenship-cessation-act-2020#sch-1-sec-36h-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "36H(4) Revocation of citizenship cessation determination on",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 18,
      "values:originalText": "(4) The Minister must give the person written notice of the Minister’s\ndecision under subsection (3). The notice must:\n\n(a) set out the decision; and\n\n(b) if the Minister refused the application:\n\n(i) include the reasons for the decision; and\n\n(ii) set out the person’s rights of review.\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\nAmendments  Part 1\n\nNo. 88, 2020\nAustralian Citizenship Amendment (Citizenship Cessation) Act 2020\n\nSection 47 (notification of decisions) does not apply in relation to a\ndecision under this section.\nNote:\nA person may seek review of a decision made under subsection (3) in\nthe High Court of Australia under section 75 of the Constitution, or in\nthe Federal Court of Australia under section 39B of the Judiciary Act\n1903."
    },
